        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಪತ್ರಿಕೋದ್ಯಮ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪತ್ರಿಕೋದ್ಯಮ — patrikōdyama — \"journalism\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅವಳು ಕಾಲೇಜಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಪತ್ರಿಕೋದ್ಯಮ ಕಲಿತಳು. avaḷu kālējinalli patrikōdyama kalitaḷu. She studied journalism at college."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪತ್ರಿಕೆ, a newspaper, and ಉದ್ಯಮ, an enterprise: the newspaper trade."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪತ್ರಿಕೋದ್ಯಮ (patrikōdyama) is borrowed from Sanskrit, a modern compound of patrikā, \"a leaf, a paper\", from pattra (CDIAL 7733), and udyama, \"undertaking, striving\" (CDIAL 2048)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
